      "title": "Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) Risk in Negative Offset Pagination",
      "body": "The `OptimizedCursorPaginator` introduces negative offset support (`start_offset = cursor.offset` when `enable_advanced_features` is true), which could allow users to access data beyond their authorized bounds. While the comment mentions permissions are checked at the queryset level, there's no explicit validation in the paginator itself to ensure the negative offset doesn't bypass authorization. This creates a potential IDOR vulnerability where users could access audit logs they shouldn't see by manipulating pagination parameters.",
      "file": "src/sentry/api/paginator.py",
      "priority": "P0"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing Input Validation for Pagination Parameters",
      "body": "The `optimized_pagination` parameter is directly used from `request.GET` without validation. While the feature is gated behind admin checks, this still represents a missing security layer. The parameter should be validated to ensure it's either 'true' or 'false' to prevent potential injection or unexpected behavior.",
      "file": "src/sentry/api/endpoints/organization_auditlogs.py",
      "priority": "P1"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent Boundary Handling in Negative Offset Logic",
      "body": "The negative offset logic in `OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_result()` has inconsistent boundary checks. When `enable_advanced_features` is true, negative offsets are allowed without proper validation of how far negative they can go. This could lead to incorrect results or performance issues when accessing very large negative offsets.",
      "file": "src/sentry/api/paginator.py",
      "priority": "P1"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing Test Coverage for Security-Critical Pagination Features",
      "body": "The diff shows no test coverage for the new negative offset functionality or the security boundaries of the optimized pagination. Given this is a security-sensitive feature (audit logs), there should be explicit tests for: 1) Negative offset behavior, 2) Permission boundaries, 3) Parameter validation, and 4) Edge cases in large datasets.",
      "file": "src/sentry/api/paginator.py",
      "priority": "P1"
    }
  ]
