    {
      "title": "Misused error return in updateDevice",
      "body": "updateDevice returns ErrDeviceLimitReached whenever rowsAffected==0 (e.g., new device_id outside the narrow time window), but this error is also used to signal the actual limit. Callers cannot distinguish the cases.",
      "file": "pkg/services/anonymous/anonimpl/anonstore/database.go",
      "priority": "P1"
    },
    {
      "title": "Beyond-limit new devices fail authentication",
      "body": "When count >= deviceLimit, a new DeviceID causes updateDevice to fail and Authenticate returns the error, rejecting anonymous auth entirely instead of allowing access without tracking.",
      "file": "pkg/services/anonymous/anonimpl/client.go",
      "priority": "P0"
    },
    {
      "title": "Synchronous TagDevice in auth path",
      "body": "Removing the goroutine makes device tagging block Authenticate (including DB calls and possible errors), a regression from the prior fire-and-forget design.",
      "file": "pkg/services/anonymous/anonimpl/client.go",
      "priority": "P1"
    },
    {
      "title": "Count + update is racy",
      "body": "No transaction between CountDevices and subsequent insert/update allows exceeding the configured deviceLimit under concurrent anonymous requests.",
      "file": "pkg/services/anonymous/anonimpl/anonstore/database.go",
      "priority": "P1"
    }
  ]
